{title: Silver Bells}
{title-keyboard: Piano}

{capo-guitar: 1}
{key: A}
{transpose-keyboard: +1}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[A2]City sidewalks, busy sidewalks
Dressed in [D2]holiday [Bm]style
In the [E]air there's a [E7]feeling
Of [A2]Christmas [E] [/F#]
[/G#]Children [A2]laughing, people passing
Meeting [D2]smile after [Bm]smile
And on [E]every street [E7]corner you'll [A2]hear [E] [/F#][/G#]

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus label="Chorus"}

[A2]Silver bells (silver bells)
[D2]Silver bells [Bm](silver bells)
[E]It's Christmas [E7]time in the [A]city [E] [/F#][/G#]
[A2]Ring-a-ling (Ring-a-ling)
[D2]Hear them ring [Bm](hear them ring)
[E]Soon it will [E7]be Christmas [A2]Day

{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[A2]Strings of streetlights, even stoplights
Blink of [D2]bright red and [Bm]green
As the [E]shoppers rush [E7]home with their [A2]treasures [E] [/F#]
[/G#]Hear the [A2]snow crunch
See the kids bunch, this is [D2]Santa’s big [Bm]scene
And a[E]bove all the [E7]bustle you'll [A2]hear [E] [/F#][/G#]

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
